# Changelog

## v0.1.0 initial version

- "Tab Hotkeys Shortcuts" proof-of-concept
- Assign numbered keyboard shortcuts to open tabs and jump to them instantly
- Tree Style Tab users can also show Jump Slot badges in the TST sidebar.
- Toolbar popup to show assigned slots
- Tab context-menu assignments and jumping

## v0.1.1 changes

- renamed to TabJump and updated description in manifest
- reduced slots from 0-9 to 1-9 to avoid using the Linux/Mac `Ctrl+0` shortcut
- allow opening of popup into a tab
- fix popup styling
- added mock browser for local popup development
- updated icon

## v0.1.2 changes

- Popup now consumes a background-owned slot view model.
- Badge style/shortcut-label computation lives in the background script.
- Popup no longer duplicates badge style constants.
- Popup display URL is shortened for layout while preserving the full URL as a tooltip.
- Fixed empty-slot title styling so assigned tab titles are not muted/italicized.
- Added viewport meta tags to popup/options/mock pages

## v0.1.3 changes

- Removed configurable Unicode badge styles.
- TST badges now render standard slot digits using CSS-controlled circular badge styling.
- Options page no longer exposes badge style configuration.
- Popup continues to consume a background-owned slot view model.
- Added a roadmap note for possible future “show assigned key” badge behavior

## v0.1.4 changes

- Added in-popup Help view.
- Added Help button beside Options.
- Added Back button from Help to Jump Slots.
- Added static default shortcut reference text.
- Added always-visible “Manage Extension Shortcuts” button in Help.
- Added simple warning if current command shortcuts differ from known defaults.
- Added open popup command with `Alt+J` / `MacCtrl+J` defaults.
- Updated Options button so it opens options and closes the popup.
- Removed the visible refresh-badges button/listener from the options UI.
- Disabling TST badges now clears existing badges immediately.
- popup digit-key jump behavior

## v0.1.5 changes

- OS-specific shortcut text in help page
- Header Help button becomes Back while viewing help.
- Shortcut key combinations in help are wrapped to prevent awkward line breaks.
- Rolled back popup digit-key jump behavior due to inability to keep popup open.
- CSS improvements and layout changes for popup

## v0.1.6 changes

- Slot number badge in the popup now acts as the Jump button.
- Popup Assign button now becomes Unassign when a slot is already assigned.
- Popup digit keys `1` through `9` jump to the assigned slot and close the popup.
- Added keyboard command for unassigning the current tab:
  - Windows/default: `Alt+Shift+0`
  - Linux: `Ctrl+Shift+0`
  - macOS: `MacCtrl+Shift+0`
- Renamed toolbar badge feedback
- Removed multi-key chord assignment from the roadmap.
- Transparent-background icon.
- Removed `popup-dev.html` and `mock-browser.js`.
- Added keyboard command for unassigning the current tab (Alt+Shift+0).
- Renamed toolbar badge feedback option to “Briefly flash tab assignments on the TabJump toolbar icon.”
- Added optional desktop notifications for slot assignment/unassignment feedback.
- Desktop notifications default off in Firefox and on in Chrome/Chromium.
- Removed multi-key chord assignment from the roadmap.

## v0.1.7 changes

- Chrome/Chromium support
  - Added platform.js compatibility layer.
  - Kept Firefox MV2 manifest as manifest.json and manifest.firefox.json.
  - Added Chrome MV3 manifest as manifest.chrome.json.
  - Added ready-to-load builds under dist/firefox and dist/chrome.
  - Updated background code for:
    - browserAction / action
    - menus / contextMenus
    - _execute_browser_action / _execute_action
    - Firefox vs Chrome shortcut settings page
    - Firefox-only TST badge behavior
- Added popup-local shortcuts:
  - Popup digit keys `1` to `9` jump to the assigned slot
  - `A` then `1`-`9` to assign,
  - `U` then `1`-`9` to unassign a slot
  - `U` then `0` to unassign the current tab.
  - `H` for Help/Back, `O` for Options
- Highlighted the slot assigned to the current tab in the popup.


## v0.1.8 suggested changes:

- Onboarding process that explains the extension and how to assign the rest of the keys for Chrome users.

## v0.2.0 changes

- Added "per-window" slot assignments option (as opposed to previous "global slot"-only assignments)
  background.js
    Added windowSlots storage.
    Added scope-aware assignment, unassignment, jumping, pruning, snapshot updating, and TST badge lookup.
    Added explicit migrations:
      migrateGlobalToPerWindow()
      migratePerWindowToGlobal(keepWindowId)
    Added per-window → global choice handling:
      getPerWindowToGlobalChoices()
      requestSlotScopeChange()
      confirmSlotScopeChange()
    Added moved-tab behavior:
      moved tab keeps its slot
      target-window slot conflict is displaced
      notification uses: Slot 3 reassigned to moved tab.
    Changed popup state to expose only the active scope’s slots.
    Made Options “clear all” able to clear all windows, while popup “Clear All” clears the current window in per-window mode.
    Fixed the TST CSS semicolon in this copy too.
  options.html
    Enabled the per-window radio option.
    Added the per-window → global confirmation panel with dropdown.
  options.js
    Scope changes now go through background migration messages.
    Ordinary option saves intentionally do not change slotScope.
    Per-window → global with 2+ assigned windows opens the dropdown chooser.
    Cancel restores the previous selected scope.
  options.css
    Added basic styling for the global-switch confirmation panel.
  popup.js
    Popup “Clear All” now sends { allWindows: false }.
    In per-window mode, the status says: Current-window slots cleared.
  Manifests
    Updated root manifest.json and manifest.chrome.json to 0.2.0.
    deprecated manifest.firefox.json
